{
 "summary": "Findings: four actionable issues remain. The first-selection key binding and cold-load guard work in focused production-controller probes, but recovery and transition handling remain incomplete.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "Title": "Give question presence ordered, lane-aware recovery",
   "Severity": "P1",
   "Location": "webview/src/client/session.ts:532-538; webview/src/client/session-readings.ts:125-130",
   "Failure": "Intent Drift. Question presence must remain authoritative after reconnects and catalog refreshes. The catalog listener refreshes questions only when active row identities change. On reconnect, seedWorkspace refreshes the catalog but leaves detailKey intact (session.ts:625-638). An unchanged catalog therefore leaves questionPresenceLoaded true with stale presence. If the original question read instead failed with RuntimeLaneLost, createReadRetry schedules no retry (src/protocol/client/background-reads.ts:96-98), leaving the flag false indefinitely. Also, refreshRowDetail replaces awaitingAnswer after awaiting a snapshot without replaying intervening question patches. The server explicitly anchors snapshots before reading their views (src/orchestration/app-service/app-service.ts:205-215), so a newer patch can be overwritten by an older snapshot. These paths can retain answered chats, erase remembered chats, or prevent a later question from reopening the offer.",
   "Fix": "Use the existing ordered session-reading family for question presence. Invalidate completeness with its lane, reseed on each new lane or invalidation independently of catalog membership, and replay newer patches over snapshots. Extend the owning session test with unchanged-catalog reconnect, lost-read recovery, and a question patch received during a snapshot."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Preserve question transitions before the app coalesces frames",
   "Severity": "P1",
   "Location": "webview/src/modules/remote/push-registration.ts:113-127",
   "Failure": "Intent Drift. A second question in a remembered chat must reopen the offer after the first answer. The listener now only refreshes registration; pruning depends on projected sessions. App coalesces ordinary session publications into one 16 ms paint (webview/src/app/app.tsx:146-168). When question.removed and question.updated arrive before that paint, the projection exposes the same waiting chat as before. Its remembered id never leaves the saved set, so the second question does not reopen the offer. A direct production-controller probe with both events before the next projected frame retained dismissed=true. The new test manually publishes each intermediate waiting set (push-registration.test.ts:209-215), so it bypasses this production ordering. The recorded listener deviation is therefore not behaviorally consistent with the approved intent.",
   "Fix": "Reconcile remembered question transitions at the ordered question-reading owner, before render-frame coalescing. Do not rely solely on a painted boolean snapshot to detect an answered-then-waiting transition. Extend the regression test to deliver both patches before the next app paint."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Do not record an unloaded waiting set when Later is pressed",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "webview/src/modules/remote/push-registration.ts:129-131",
   "Failure": "Boundary Discipline. Later must remember the chats already waiting when the person dismisses the offer. The read-side reconciliation checks questionPresenceLoaded, but dismiss() does not. PushGuide permits Later once registration permission state resolves, independently of question loading (webview/src/modules/remote/push-guide.tsx:15,40). On a slow question read, pressing Later records an empty set. When the existing waiting chat arrives, lines 124-125 classify it as new and immediately remove the dismissal. A production-controller probe reproduced dismissed=false after resolving presence for the already-waiting chat.",
   "Fix": "Defer committing the dismissal baseline until authoritative question presence arrives, while retaining the person's dismissal. Alternatively, make the action unavailable until that baseline exists. Add this ordering to the owning dismissal test."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Do not clear Later for questions that arrive while notifications are on",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "webview/src/modules/remote/push-registration.ts:124-126",
   "Failure": "Scope of Invalidation. The offer must return only when a chat starts waiting while notifications from this machine are off. The reconciliation removes the remembered dismissal for every newly waiting chat, including when registration.state().kind is on. After notifications are disabled later, the offer appears without any chat starting to wait while notifications were off. A production-controller probe reproduced this sequence: dismiss, enable successfully, add a waiting chat, revoke permission. The final state was denied with dismissed=false.",
   "Fix": "Gate dismissal invalidation on notification availability for this machine. Advance the remembered waiting baseline while notifications are on so a later permission change does not reinterpret an earlier question as a new off-state transition. Add this sequence to the owning test."
  }
 ],
